<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_LineVolunteer — UNFINISHED_LINE_WORLD_FOUNDRY_1 (design droid_mass_production_quest_chain_2026-10-02.md §4.2
  "Volunteers", §4.4 brake 4). Owner Q1=A, 2026-10-03.

  THE SPEC (rimworld-quests §2):
    ask       take in one free Enclave droid who has chosen to join the clan
    reason    the line gave a fallen Enclave head a new body, and the droid wants to work among the people who
              helped build that line
    choice    accept a hand who must stay free, or let the offer lapse
    failure   none inside the quest. The stake is outside it: bolting or wiping the volunteer later collapses
              Enclave goodwill and closes the line to you (WorldComponent_RUT_EnclaveFoundry.CheckBetrayal)
    reward    the droid itself; no silver
    deadline  the offer window (expireDaysRange); nothing to complete after acceptance

  FIRING: route 4-shaped (code). WorldComponent_RUT_EnclaveFoundry.TryOfferVolunteer generates it on its own timer
  while the line runs, the Enclaves are allied and the cap is not reached (Mod Settings: volunteerDays,
  volunteerCap). isRootSpecial + weight 0 so the storyteller never offers it. Dev: Debug actions -> Quests ->
  "Unfinished Line: offer a line volunteer now".

  NOT a spine beat and no epicParent: the spine (RUT_UnfinishedLine) has already ended when the line stands, and
  epicParent is read only by QuestNode_Root_RelicHunt (RimSage, decompiled 1.6) - it would nest nothing.

  SHAPE: beat 1's (RUT_UnfinishedLine_1_Count) pawn generation and QuestNode_PawnsArrive joinPlayer, without the
  return trip. QuestNode_RUT_LineVolunteers with no inSignal arms on acceptance and hands the droid to the foundry
  watch, which strips any bolt/wipe mark a generator left on it. The droid kinds are beat 1's four Droidworks
  civilian kinds (the Enclave faction's own kinds still MayRequire Droid Depot).
  PROVISIONAL: expireDaysRange 4~6, the 2500-tick settle before the quest closes.
-->
<Defs>

  <QuestScriptDef>
    <defName>RUT_LineVolunteer</defName>
    <isRootSpecial>true</isRootSpecial>
    <rootSelectionWeight>0</rootSelectionWeight>
    <expireDaysRange>4~6</expireDaysRange>
    <everAcceptableInSpace>true</everAcceptableInSpace>

    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->A hand off the line</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>

    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->[volunteers0_nameDef] fell once, and [enclaveFaction_name] kept [volunteers0_possessive] head. The line you helped build has given [volunteers0_objective] a body again, and [volunteers0_nameDef] has asked to walk to your camp and work beside the Jawa.\n\nNobody is sending [volunteers0_objective]; the choice was [volunteers0_possessive] own, and the Enclaves will be watching what the choice costs. A volunteer comes free and stays free: put a restraining bolt in [volunteers0_objective], or wipe [volunteers0_possessive] memory, and the line will not run for you again.</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>

    <root Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
      <nodes>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetMap" />
        <li Class="QuestNode_GetWalkInSpot" />

        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.UnfinishedLine.QuestNode_RUT_GetLineFactions">
          <storeEnclaveAs>enclaveFaction</storeEnclaveAs>
          <storeHiveAs>hiveFaction</storeHiveAs>
          <storeSettlementAs>settlement</storeSettlementAs>
        </li>

        <!-- One volunteer. addToList, so [volunteers0_*] text and volunteers.* signals hang on the list var. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_RandomNode">
          <nodes>
            <li Class="QuestNode_GeneratePawn"><kindDef>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_T3UD</kindDef><faction>$enclaveFaction</faction><addToList>volunteers</addToList><ensureNonNumericName>true</ensureNonNumericName></li>
            <li Class="QuestNode_GeneratePawn"><kindDef>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_R8009UD</kindDef><faction>$enclaveFaction</faction><addToList>volunteers</addToList><ensureNonNumericName>true</ensureNonNumericName></li>
            <li Class="QuestNode_GeneratePawn"><kindDef>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GE3LD</kindDef><faction>$enclaveFaction</faction><addToList>volunteers</addToList><ensureNonNumericName>true</ensureNonNumericName></li>
            <li Class="QuestNode_GeneratePawn"><kindDef>RSW_DW_KotORDroidGood_3C</kindDef><faction>$enclaveFaction</faction><addToList>volunteers</addToList><ensureNonNumericName>true</ensureNonNumericName></li>
          </nodes>
        </li>

        <!-- On acceptance: the droid walks in and joins. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_PawnsArrive">
          <pawns>$volunteers</pawns>
          <joinPlayer>true</joinPlayer>
          <customLetterLabel TKey="LetterLabelLineVolunteerArrived">A hand off the line</customLetterLabel>
          <customLetterText TKey="LetterTextLineVolunteerArrived">[volunteers0_nameDef] has walked in from the flats in a body that still smells of the line. No bolt sits in [volunteers0_possessive] chassis, and [volunteers0_nameDef] asks for none.\n\nThe Enclaves gave this one freely. They will take everything back if you treat [volunteers0_objective] as property.</customLetterText>
        </li>

        <!-- On acceptance: hand the volunteer to the foundry watch (bolt/wipe = betrayal). -->
        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.UnfinishedLine.QuestNode_RUT_LineVolunteers">
          <pawns>$volunteers</pawns>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_Delay">
          <delayTicks>2500</delayTicks>
          <outSignalComplete>VolunteerSettled</outSignalComplete>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>VolunteerSettled</inSignal>
          <outcome>Success</outcome>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>map.MapRemoved</inSignal>
          <outcome>InvalidPreAcceptance</outcome>
          <signalListenMode>NotYetAcceptedOnly</signalListenMode>
        </li>

      </nodes>
    </root>
  </QuestScriptDef>

</Defs>
